From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:14:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(render): a sibling change restyles hosts whose shadow
 sheets test their position

`:host(:first-child)` and `:host(:nth-child())` live in the host's own
shadow sheet, but a light-DOM insert or remove looked up structural rules
only in the sheets that select the parent's children, so a host that moved
from first to second kept its first-child style until a full cascade. The
structural scopes of a child-list change now also consult the shadow sheets
of the parent's child hosts.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
